// Typed Abla implementation of ESP-IDF's configured ESP32 panic unit. Normal
// control flow, printing, state access, watchdog handling, reset hints, and
// callback dispatch stay in the monolithic LLVM graph. Only MMIO, the Xtensa
// core-id/debug registers, semihosting break, and terminal trap are target
// operations.

// These linker-visible storage regions are shared with the still-typed-by-ABI
// panic entry and task-watchdog units. The strings are addressed directly so
// an emergency handler never constructs boxed Abla strings on its stack. This
// block declares data only; it contains no processor instructions. Once those
// units use direct Abla references, the final object-format aliases can become
// native statics.


